    "1 · Connect Claude Code, in %@’s folder": {},
    "1. Find the app target that ships: the one whose PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER is %@ (fill in $(…) references and settings from .xcconfig files; with a workspace, look in each .xcodeproj).\n2. Add the key the way that target is set up. When it has GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE = YES, add the build setting to every build configuration of that target (Debug, Release and any other), beside its other INFOPLIST_KEY_ settings in project.pbxproj, or in the .xcconfig file its configurations use when that's where they are. Otherwise add the key to the Info.plist its INFOPLIST_FILE names, in the file's own format. Not both. When a key isn't one this Xcode generates from an INFOPLIST_KEY_ setting, put it in the target's Info.plist instead.\n3. Leave other targets alone: extensions, widgets, frameworks and test targets ship inside the app's upload, and App Store Connect asks the question once for it. Only an embedded app with its own bundle that App Store Connect reads in the upload too, such as a watchOS app, gets the same key the same way; name it in where.\n4. When the key is already there with %@, change nothing and report alreadyThere. When it says the other value, change it to %@ (the answer is settled in Atlas), report added, and say in notes what it was.\n5. Check it: plutil -lint <the Info.plist>, or xcodebuild -showBuildSettings for the target. Don't build, archive or upload: the person uploads the next build.": {},
