    "Design": {},
    "Design project": {},
    "Design project “%@”": {},
    "Design system or project": {},
    "Design the art for %@’s In-App Event “%@” (app %@, event %@) in Atlas with Claude Design: its card (16:9) and its details page (9:16). Read the event with get_in_app_events (eventId %@, include [\"all\"]): its badge, texts, dates, which languages lack their own card or details page, and `design`, the app's look and design language, what Atlas knows of the app, its design project and the art direction (the idea, where the App Store lays its text, the craft and the check of each render). If `design` says the look is missing, read it in the project and send it with report_app_support first. When the design project opens from here, design in it; when it doesn't, design from what `design` gives, and never stop for it. Look at how the project draws its own visuals (scenes, backgrounds, motifs, animated loops) with Glob, Grep and Read, so the art belongs to the app and to the event's theme. Make each piece one page of HTML, CSS and inline SVG at the canvas size, crafted as the art direction says, with motion as CSS or SVG animation that loops seamlessly over 20 seconds (JavaScript doesn't run, and nothing loads from the web), and render it with render_event_artwork and motion: true for a video, or without motion for a still. When the project renders its own scenes and you can run that, you may render a piece with it instead and send the file with curl -s --data-binary @<file> '<artworkUpload link>?name=<file name>'. No words or logos in the art, and no border or gradient overlay of your own: the App Store lays its own fade under the text, while color that belongs to the scene, like a sky, is fine. Keep the lower part dark and quiet, where Apple lays the badge, name and description, but still part of the scene. Look at each render under the event's text, check it against the art direction's selfCheck, and fix what fails, every refusal and the warnings you can. Then queue the card and the details page with propose_event_artwork for the languages that need them (the primary language's shows in the others). Never push and never submit the event for review: the person accepts and pushes it.": {},
