    "Each assistant gets its own token, which you can revoke in Settings → AI Assistants.": {},
    "Each caption is measured as it arrives. Ones that don’t fit are flagged, never cut. Accepted text stays tagged “machine-translated” until someone reviews it.": {},
    "Each concept adapts one of the person’s templates: set template to %@.": {},
    "Each concept keeps its drawing and gets a %lld-second loop. You can open the ones that are ready.": {},
    "Each concept shows up here as it’s done. You can open the ones that are ready.": {},
    "Each currency’s usual ending": {},
    "Each event is a card people see in search, in Today and on %@’s page. Open one to write it, give it artwork and send it to App Review.": {},
    "Each item needs a locale of the plan, a slot from 1 to %lld and a headline.": {},
    "Each item’s `screen` is one of the default set’s screens, 1 to %lld, as get_page_screenshots lists them.": {},
    "Each language's screenshots, with their suggested captions": {},
    "Each of setupCommands is run as it is, so it’s one line starting with xcrun or xcodebuild, and “%@” isn’t. A switch like TEST_RUNNER_X=1 belongs in the scheme’s Test action or test plan, and an instruction goes in setupNotes.": {},
    "Each period": {},
    "Each region’s equalized prices are multiplied by its factor, then snapped to Apple’s price points.": {},
    "Each request carries a short-lived token (ES256, 15 minutes) signed on this Mac with the private key.": {},
