    "Make an event’s deep link work": {},
    "Make an image for %@'s retention message \"%@\" in Atlas with Claude, in the app's design language: a PNG 3840 pixels wide and 1000 tall (160 to 2160 is allowed), no transparency, that reads on Apple's Confirm Cancellation screen in light and in dark mode, with no text in it. Save it in %@, then call propose_retention_message for that message with kind \"image\" and the PNG as imageBase64 (Atlas is sandboxed and may not read the file at imagePath).": {},
    "Make it available in new countries and regions automatically": {},
    "Make it work in the project: declare the URL scheme or domain when it's missing, handle the link, and open the event's screen. Build it for a simulator and test it with xcrun simctl openurl booted '<link>', on a cold launch and with the app open. Then bump the build number (CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION) by one, so the next upload carries it, and don't archive or upload the build: the person uploads it.": {},
    "Make its pages with the pages prompt and send them with propose_artwork_concept, concept {\"id\": \"%@\"} and artworkDesign: %@ still to come.": {},
    "Make new screenshots, an App Preview and header artwork in 3 short steps. Autopilot does the rest and asks you only to choose the look and to review.": {},
    "Make the %@ simulator in Xcode › Window › Devices and Simulators, then retry.": {},
