    "Set its price in the United States; every other country or region gets Apple’s equalized price, which you can change here after the push.": {},
    "Set them in App Store Connect: Atlas can’t change this event’s dates.": {},
    "Set them under Details.": {},
    "Set to Feel Like %@": {},
    "Set up %@": {},
    "Set up Apple's Retention Messaging API for %@, step by step, asking me before each change. 1. Find the app's server code. 2. Add the Get Retention Message endpoint Apple calls when someone taps Cancel: it must answer within 700 ms with the message to show (by its ID in App Store Connect), an alternate product to suggest, or a promotional offer signed with the app's In-App Purchase key; when it can't, Apple shows the messages set up in App Store Connect. 3. Verify Apple's signed requests. 4. Register the sandbox URL with the Retention Messaging API and run Apple's performance test. 5. Tell me what's left for production. Don't put any key in the code, and don't call App Store Connect's write APIs.": {},
    "Set up a starting price for %@. Every other country or region gets Apple’s equalized price.": {},
    "Set up availability": {},
    "Set up the app’s price": {},
    "Set up the subscriptions of %@ in Atlas. Read the app's project for what it sells: the product IDs its StoreKit code or .storekit configuration buys, each one's duration, and what the paywall says it unlocks. Check get_subscriptions for what App Store Connect already has, then propose each missing subscription with propose_subscription: its group, reference name, the product ID exactly as the code uses it, duration, display name and description, and a starting price in US dollars (the paywall's or the .storekit file's when there is one). Propose a lifetime unlock or other one-time purchase with propose_in_app_purchase, and a free trial or intro price the paywall promises with propose_introductory_offer. For a subscription App Store Connect has, propose the promotional offers (by the identifier the code passes to StoreKit), win-back offers and offer codes the code or its marketing uses with propose_promotional_offer, propose_win_back_offer and propose_offer_code. Every product needs an App Review screenshot of the paywall: send the image to get_subscriptions' reviewScreenshotUploadURL and pass its fileId as reviewScreenshot, or later with propose_purchase_review_screenshot. Pass evidence as \"file:line — finding\". Don't propose what's already there. %@": {},
