    "The person keeps these screens: send their steps without replace.": {},
    "The person liked the concepts for %@’s In-App Event “%@” (app %@, event %@) and asked for them to move: %@. Read get_event_artwork_brief: its addMotion has each concept’s two pages and its motionDirection has Apple’s rules for event videos and how the loop should move. Keep every drawing exactly as it is and add CSS or SVG animation to its pages: one thing that tells the event moves, slowly, the camera stays put, the first frame is complete on its own and nothing flashes. Check each page with render_event_artwork and motionFrames: true, fix what its loop check says, then send each concept with propose_event_artwork_concept and replaces, one call each. Never push and never submit the event.": {},
    "The person looked at the screenshots Atlas made for the custom product page “%@” of %@ (app %@) and asked for a change: “%@”. Read get_page_screenshots with page “%@”: its run has the plan and the change. Change only what they asked and send the plan again with propose_page_screenshots: every screen in the new order, with every language’s captions for the ones whose words change (the others keep theirs). Atlas lays the set out again. Never push and never submit the page.": {},
    "The person made the test already: it’s theirs to change in App Store Connect.": {},
    "The person queued “%@” themselves and hasn’t pushed it. Leave Export Compliance to them.": {},
    "The person said Not Now to a %@ page for %@. Leave %@ out unless they add it.": {},
    "The person said what they expect of the header and search: %@. Make sure this direction's pages show it, then send followsTheRequest: in a sentence, what in them answers it.": {},
    "The person sees it as Not offered and can't accept it: write another for this language.": {},
    "The person stopped receiving this run’s suggestions in Atlas. Don’t send more for it.": {},
    "The person types the demo account’s password in Atlas: it’s never read or sent over MCP.": {},
    "The person wants a new look for the screenshots of the custom product page “%@” of %@ (app %@): three looks to choose from, made for this page’s audience. Work in this order.\n1. Read get_page_screenshots with page “%@”: who the page is for, the plan and its captions, and `look`. Read get_template for the default page’s template: its fields, fonts and per-slot designs.\n2. Design three looks that are clearly different from the default page’s and from each other (background, colors, caption type, device frame), that read well in every language of the page, and that still feel like %@. Design them as Atlas templates from get_template’s fields: Claude Design and Figma can’t be opened from here.\n3. Send each with propose_page_look: a name, a one-sentence rationale, base (default for the default page’s template, or a starter) and the template fields or ops that change. Look at the preview it returns; send a look again with the same name to fix it.\nNever push and never submit the page: the person chooses one of the three in Atlas.": {},
